{"id":"000W2X","title":"Fireflines: Whisper in the Dark","author":"dawsonjones2020","solvedCount":0,"difficulty":3,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-17T04:36:41+00:00","posted":"Heute, 05:05 Uhr","rules":"This puzzle is the third in a series exploring the firefly ruleset. I hope you enjoy! If you do, feel free to leave a comment and check out my other puzzles!\n\nSolve on SudokuPad\n\nRules\n\nSudoku: Each row, column, and 3×3 box contains the digits 1–9 once each.\n\nFirefly: For each circle, draw a path starting from its black dot, moving through the centers of cells, and ending at a circle (potentially the same one it started at), but not on the side containing another black dot. Paths may not cross themselves, each other, or pass through circles. A number in a circle represents how many turns the path exiting from its dot will make. All circles must be joined by paths to form one connected network.\n\nGerman Whispers: Adjacent digits along each firefly path must differ by at least 5. This includes both the starting and ending circles.\n\nWhite Kropki: Digits connected by a white dot are consecutive.\n\nIf you're not familiar with the firefly rules and would like some examples click here","solutionCode":"Digits on a path in row 4, followed by digits on a path in row 5.","tags":["Sudoku"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/ndf9gwzz06","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/ndf9gwzz06","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["overlays","underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-17T04:36:41+00:00"}